                <pb facs="0775" n="657" xml:id="pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.77/249: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-01T17:00:00-05:45">November 1, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>260. In view of the information contained in the Department’s telegram 148,
                    October 31, 11 a.m., President Moncada told me this morning that he will proceed
                    on the assumption that the White Corporation will continue its management of the
                    railroad until the end of this year.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
